  "question": {
    "text": "The least value of n for which the number of integral terms in the Binomial expansion of \\((\\sqrt[3]{7}+\\sqrt[12]{11})^{\\mathrm{n}}\\) is 183, is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "7MTBr",
      "text": "2184",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PVn9S",
      "text": "2196",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "QyJdD",
      "text": "2148",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JXfrl",
      "text": "2172",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\text { General term }={ }^{\\mathrm{n}} \\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{r}}\\left\\{7^{1 / 3}\\right\\}^{\\mathrm{n}-\\mathrm{r}}\\left(11^{1 / 12}\\right)^{\\mathrm{r}} \\\\\n& ={ }^{\\mathrm{n}} \\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{r}}\\{7\\}^{\\frac{\\mathrm{n}-\\mathrm{r}}{3}}(11)^{\\mathrm{r} / 12}\n\\end{aligned}$\n\nFor integral terms, r must be multiple of 12\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{r}=12 \\mathrm{k}, \\mathrm{k} \\in \\mathrm{~W}$\n\nTotal values of $r=183$\nHence $\\max r=12(182)$\n$=2184$\n\nMin value of $n=2184$",
    "image": null
  },
